8. THESIS-READY SUMMARY PARAGRAPH
============================================================================================
  Under ordered input on the Flink architecture (n = 3120 messages, 52 windows,
  4 runs), median end-to-end latency is 35.6 s (p99 = 65.4 s, max = 67.3 s).
  Run-to-run variability is below 2%.  The latency distribution is approximately
  uniform on [6 s, 67 s], a direct consequence of Flink's 1-minute event-time
  tumbling window: each consecutive message in a window waits 1 s less than the
  previous, giving a per-position slope of -1 s.  After subtracting the
  deterministic windowing wait, the pure infrastructure overhead is 6.2 +/- 2.6 s
  per message, of which ~5 s is the coordinator's idle-flush timeout
  (consumer.receive(5000)).

